   "raw": "Page 1\nODU-MT7981_V.1\nCPU\nMediaTek MT7981\nRAM\n512MB\nFLASH\n32MB\nWAN\n1x 10/100\nCellular\nM.2 Quectel EC200A LTE 4G module\nSIM\n2x Nano SIM (1x Active & 1x Passive)\nWi-Fi\nNA\nRTC\nBuilt-in RTC\nReset\nPinhole Reset Button\nAntenna\nCellular: 2x N Type Connector\nStatus LED\n1x Power, 1x Sys, 1x Mode, 1x ACT, 2x Program, 8x Signal Strength, 2x SIM, 5x\nEthernet\nPower Connector\nPoE in\nInput Voltage Range\n802.3af (48V-57V)\nPower Adapter\nYes\nEnclosure\nPolycarbonate IP66 Housing\nMounting\nWALL Mount\nDesign\nFanless\nDimensions\n140 x 84 x 224 mm (W x H x D)\nWeight\n950 gm\nStorage Temperature\n-20 ~ 60 °C\nOperating Temperature\n-0 ~ 50 °C\nHumidity\n10 ~ 90% (non-condensing)\nODU-MT7981\nDATA SHEET\nPRODUCT INFO\nPROCESSOR\nMediaTek MT7981, 512MB DDR RAM, 128MB NAND\nCELLULAR\n4G/3G/2G with Dual SIM, External 5dBi antenna\n5G Ready (Support for 5G in case of 5G requirement)\nWi-Fi\nNA\nINTERFACE\n1x WAN 10/100\nPOWER\nPoE IN (802.3af (48V-57V))\nOPERATING SYSTEM\nOpen-WRT Linux\nHardware Specification\nOperational & Environmental\nPage 2\nODU-MT7981_V.1\nSOFTWARE SPECIFICATIONS\nCellular Module\n4G (LTE) - Cat 4 up to 150 Mbps, 3G - up to 42 Mbps, 2G - up to 236.8 Kbps\nStatus\nSingle strength (RSSI), SINR, RSRP, RSRQ\nBand Management\nAuto/User configurable\nOperator Lock\nAutomatic/Mannual\nAPN\nConfigurable, Auto APN\nModem configuration mode\nSingle SIM, Dual SIM\nSIM switching\nSignal strength, ICMP echo, Data limit based\nPDP Type\nIPv4, IPv6, IPv4v6\nSIM Authentication\nPAP,CHAP, No Authentication\nSMS\nSend SMS, Read SMS, SMS Commands\nRouting\nStatic routing, Advanced Static Routing\nNetwork Protocols\nTCP, UDP, IPv4, IPv6, ICMP, NTP, HTTP, HTTPS, SCP, PPP, SSH, DHCP\nConnection Monitoring\nPing Reboot, Scheduled Periodic Reboot\nFirewall features\nPort forward, traffic rules, SNAT, Zone forwarding, Parental Control,\nMasquerading, MSS Clamping, Loopback IP, Loopback Rules.\nAttack Prevention\nSYN Flood Protection, Drop Invalid Packets\nDHCP\nStatic and Dynamic\nMulti-WAN Configuration\nConfigurable Failover, load balancing between Cellular WAN, Wi-Fi WAN and\nWired.\nVLAN\nTagged VLAN, Untagged VLAN\nVPN\nOpen VPN, IPsec, GRE, L2TP, PPTP, Wireguard, Zero Tier, IPIP Tunnel\nOpen VPN\nTUN/TAP with TLS Certificates\nIPsec\nIKEv1, IKEv2, Aggressive/Main Mode\nIPsec Encryption\n3DES, AES128, AES192, AES256\nIPsec Authentication\nSHA1, MD5, SHA256, SHA384, SHA512\nIPsec DH Group\nMODP768, MODP1024, MODP1536, MODP2048, MODP3072, MODP4096\nPPTP/L2TP\nServer & Client with/without MPPE Encryption\nMonitoring Application\nModem Monitoring with ICMP Echo, Router Monitoring with ICMP Echo\nTime Synchronization\nNTP Client, RTC, Manual\nDiagnostic\nPing, Traceroute, Modem Debug Info, Iperf, Download Logs\nOther Features\nMAC binding, Connection Diagnostics, URL Filtering, Router Health\nMonitoring, Package Manager\nNMS\nRemote Monitoring & Management Platform for SILBO Networking products\nNMS VPN\nRemote Access of SILBO and non-SILBO Networking Devices\nTR069\nTR069 Client for CPE Management\nSMS Commands\nReboot Command, Uptime Command\nOperating System\nOpen-WRT based Linux OS\nSupported Languages\nShell scripting, C, C++\nDevelopment tools\nSDK package with built environment provided (Optional)\nODU-MT7981-Outdoor Cellular Router with Polycarbonate IP66 Housing , 2x External Antennas, PoE Injector*, Mounting Kit.\nCellular\nFirewall & Networking\nOperating System\nStandard Packaging\nRemote Management\nPage 3\nODU-MT7981_V.1\n*Star-marked features on the SILBO ODU-MT7981-Outdoor cellular router are accessible only after opening Top panel/ cover of the IP66 housing.\nSPATIAL MEASUREMENT:\nTop View\n*All rights reserved, subject to change without prior notice.\nGet in touch:\nsales@invendis.com\nwww.silbonetworks.com\nInvendis Technologies India Private Limited\nNo. 230, 1st Cross, 38th Main, BOOHBCS Layout, BTM\n2nd Stage, Bangalore – 560 068\n224 mm\n140 mm"
